<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<osis xmlns="http://www.bibletechnologies.net/2003/OSIS/namespace" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.bibletechnologies.net/2003/OSIS/namespace http://www.bibletechnologies.net/osisCore.2.1.1.xsd">
  <osisText osisIDWork="REV_Sloane273_Translation" osisRefWork="bible" xml:lang="en">
    <header>
      <work osisWork="REV_Sloane273_Translation">
        <title>English Translation of Revelation (British Library MS Sloane 273)</title>
        <identifier type="OSIS">REV_Sloane273_Translation</identifier>
        <scope>REV</scope>
        <language>en</language>
        <type type="x-translation">Translation</type>
        <identifier type="shelfmark">British Library, MS Sloane 273</identifier>
        <contributor role="trl" file-as="Gordon, Nehemia">Nehemia Gordon</contributor>
        <date event="eversion" type="ISO">2017</date>
        <rights>© 2017 Nehemia Gordon</rights>
        <description>Hebrew transcription and English translation of the Revelation passages in British Library MS Sloane 273, transcribed and translated by Nehemia Gordon.</description>
      </work>
      <work osisWork="bible">
        <identifier type="OSIS">bible</identifier>
        <refSystem>StandardV11N</refSystem>
        <language>en</language>
      </work>
    </header>
    <div type="book" osisID="Rev">
      <chapter osisID="Rev.1">
        <verse osisID="Rev.1.1" n="1">( The vision of Yehoshua Mashiach, that the Elohim gave him to show his servants that which was necessary to be with wrath, and he taught (horah) sending by the hand of his angel to his servant Yochanan.<note type="footnote" n="2">יִׁנֵשׁ רַעַשַה The Second Gate</note> </verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.1.2" n="2">( That he testified the word of the Elohim and the witness of Yehoshua Mashiach, which he saw, and that are here,3 and that which was necessary to do<note type="footnote" n="3">The word הָנֵה "here" appears four times in the text, perhaps having the idiosyncratic meaning of "these".</note> </verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.1.3" n="3">after this. Happy is the man who reads and the ones who hear the words of the prophecy and guard here, those that are written in it. For the time is near.</verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.1.4" n="4">Yochanan to the seven congregations, that are in Asia. Grace to you and Shalom from him who is, and who will be, and who will come and from the seven souls that are opposite his throne.</verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.1.5" n="5">( And from Yehoshua Mashiach who is the witness of faithfulness. the firstborn of the men and the prince of the kings of the Earth, who loved us and baptized us from our sins<note type="footnote" n="4">Literally, "men" based on the vowels in the manuscript. "Firstborn of the dead" would be םיִׁתֵמַה.</note> </verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.1.6" n="6">with his blood. ( And he made us a kingdom and priests to Elohim and his Father. To him is glory and dominion, forever. Amen.</verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.1.7" n="7">and these that stabbed him. And they will mourn him, all the tribes of the Earth. Also, Amen.<note type="footnote" n="5">Should be הֶלֵאְּו.</note> </verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.1.8" n="8">( I am the Aleph and the Tav, says Yehovah the Elohim. He that is, and he was will be, and he that will come, the Shaddai.</verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.1.9" n="9">( I am Yochanan your brother and a participant in the suffering, and in the kingdom, and in the hope in Mashiach Yehoshua. I was on the island that is called Patmos for the word of the Elohim and for the testimony of</verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.1.10" n="10">Yehoshua Mashiach. ( I was in the spirit on the lordly6 day<note type="footnote" n="6">The unique form יִׁיִׁנֹּדֲא is apparently an adjective derived from יָנֹּדֲא or יִׁנֹּדֲא.</note> </verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.1.11" n="11">a trumpet, (11) that says, That which you see, write in a book, and send to the seven congregations, to Ephesus, and to Smyrna, and to Pergamus, and to Thyatira, and to Sardis, and to Philadelphia, and to Laodicea.</verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.1.12" n="12">( And there I turned to look at the voice that spoke with me. And I was turning and saw seven golden lamps.</verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.1.13" n="13">( And in the middle of the seven lamps dominion for the Son of Man, dressed with a tunic</verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.1.14" n="14">( And his head and the hairs are white like bright wool,</verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.1.15" n="15">like snow, and his eyes like a flame of fire. ( And his feet are likened to polished copper, when glowing in the furnace. And his voice is like the sound of the deep- sea.<note type="footnote" n="7">The Shin-dot is missing in the manuscript.</note> </verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.1.16" n="16">( And he is holding in his right hand seven stars. And from his mouth goes forth a double-edged sword. And his face is like the light of the sun</verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.1.17" n="17">in its strength. ( And when I saw him, I fell to his feet like a dead person. And he put his right hand on me and he said, Do not be afraid.</verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.1.18" n="18">and behold I live forever and ever. Amen. And I have the nails</verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.1.19" n="19">of death and She'ol. (19) Therefore, write that which you saw, and that are here, and that which is necessary to do after this.</verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.1.20" n="20">( The secret of the seven stars that you saw in my right hand and the seven golden lamps, the seven stars are angels of the seven congregations and the seven lamps that you saw, are the seven congregations. [they are] The Second Gate<note type="footnote" n="8">Should be הָמֵה.</note> </verse>
      </chapter>
      <chapter osisID="Rev.2">
        <verse osisID="Rev.2.1" n="1">To the angel of the congregation of Ephesus, write here: The one who is holding the seven stars in his right hand and that walks in the middle of the seven</verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.2.2" n="2">golden lamps says. ( I know your labors, and toil, and abundant patience, and that you are not able to bear evil ones. And you tested it, those who say that they are sent and they are not and you found<note type="footnote" n="9">The extraneous Kamatz is in the manuscript.</note> <note type="footnote" n="10">The Shin-dot is missing in the manuscript.</note> <note type="footnote" n="11">Should be: םָתא צְּמוּ.</note> </verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.2.3" n="3">them to be liars. ( And you took and you have abundant patience for my name's sake and you have not</verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.2.4" n="4">perished. ( But I have something against you for you left</verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.2.5" n="5">your first love. ( And remember from where you were thrown down and repent and do the first deeds. And if not, I will come to you as a sudden surprise. And I will shake your lamp<note type="footnote" n="12">This Sin-dot is missing in the manuscript.</note> </verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.2.6" n="6">from its place, if you do not repent. ( But you have this, that you hate the deed of the Nicolaitans</verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.2.7" n="7">that I also hate. ( He who has an ear will hear what the spirit says to congregations. I will let the victorious eat of the tree of life, which is in the divine orchard (pardes).<note type="footnote" n="13">Cholam is missing in the manuscript.</note> </verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.2.8" n="8">( And write for the angel of the congregation of Smyrna and here, say, the first and the last that was dead</verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.2.9" n="9">and lives. ( I know your deeds and the suffering and the poverty, but you are rich. and the despising of those who speak to be Judaic14 and they are not, but rather the council of the satan.<note type="footnote" n="14">Yehudiyim is an adjective meaning "Judaic" and distinct from Yehudim, the normal word for "Jews". Yehudiyim was understood as referring to the Ten Lost Tribes who labeled themselves "Judaic", but not "Jewish". This is referred to in Genesis Rabbah, Vayechi, Section 97, "also in this world you will be honored that all the tribes will call themselves Yehudiyim, just as you are called Yehudah" " ףא הדוהי התא תארקנש םשכ ,םיידוהי ךמש לע םיטבשה לכ וארקיש הכזת הזה םלועב".</note> </verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.2.10" n="10">( Do not be afraid for suffering was necessary. And behold destruction (Avadon) will give some of you to the prison to test you. And you will have suffering for ten days. Be faithful until death and I will give you the crown</verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.2.11" n="11">of life. ( He who has an ear will hear what the spirit says to the congregations. The one who overcomes will not</verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.2.12" n="12">be smitten by the Second Death. ( And to the angel of the congregation in Pergamus write here saying, To he who has the double-edged Cherub15<note type="footnote" n="15">Presumably בֶרֶכַה "the Cherub" is a scribal error for בֶרֶחַה "the sword".</note> </verse>
        <verse osisID="Rev.2.13" n="13">( I know your deeds and where he is sitting, where the seat of Satan is</verse>
      </chapter>
    </div>
  </osisText>
</osis>
